 # Distance Field Representations and Sampling
 
-Also called: Distance Field Sampling, Distance Field Traversal
 
 ## Overview
-This family defines the mechanisms for querying scalar fields that represent implicit surfaces or volumetric data via distance metrics, enabling ray marching and spatial queries. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods by focusing on the *sampling interface* and *data structures* required to evaluate these fields efficiently, rather than the geometric primitives themselves. While [SDF Primitive Definitions](1578-sdf-primitive-definitions.md) provides the analytical building blocks, this family addresses how those blocks are stored (textures, grids, neural networks) and accessed (bounded lookups, probabilistic outputs, haptic constraints) in a rendering or simulation pipeline.
